{
  "about": "The launch video's cut (sample 1, English). entries: the timeline in order; a shot's in/out are seconds of its recording (trailer-out/shots/<shot>.mp4), a plate's card is drawn for `seconds`. cards: the text drawn by titles.html (index = trailer-out/cards/<n>.png); an entry's `cards` lay them over it from..to (seconds into the entry), faded `fade` s. music: the soundtrack (`path`, from the repo root; the user's piece, kept out of git in trailer-out/music) or pieces of assets/music (`file`), by timeline second (at, until) or over a run of entries (`entries`: [first, last]); the clips' own music is never heard, only their ambience and physics. sfx: which game samples (src/audio/samples) each physics event kind sounds as; ambience: loops under each shot. Read by tools/trailer/assemble.py.",
